1000 GOSUB 6105:BM$="The fortune teller's house was wrapped in black curtains. It was so dimly\lit that David and Susanna were forced to walk carefully, so as not to\stumble.":GOSUB 5100
1010 BM$="The voice of a man came from the back.":GOSUB 5100
1020 BM$="`Open the curtains.`":GOSUB 5100
1030 GOSUB 6110:BM$="David did as told, and peered inside.":GOSUB 5100
1040 BM$="The room beyond was also shrouded in black curtains. A single lit candle on\the table provided a small source of light.\There were no signs of the owner of the voice.":GOSUB 5100
1050 BM$="`Approach the table.`":GOSUB 5100
1060 GOSUB 6120:BM$="David and Susanna approached the table, as told.":GOSUB 5100
1070 BM$="`Well met. I am Michael, the fortune teller.`":GOSUB 5100
1075 GOSUB 6123:GOSUB 6121
1080 BM$="The candle flickered at Michael's words. It was as if the voice came from\the candle itself.":GOSUB 5100
