1300 BM$="Michael: It seems you've been looking for someone.":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1310 BM$="Susanna: How did he know? We didn't say anything yet!":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1320 BM$="Michael: I am no mere fortune teller. I am a real sorcerer, wielder of dark\magicks.":GOSUB 5100
1330 BM$="At the mention of dark magicks, David wondered if he wasn't in another\one of his dreams.":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1340 BM$="Susanna: David, what should we do? I'm scared...":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1350 BM$="Michael: There is nothing to be afraid of. Simply tell me the age and the\name of the person you're looking for. If you've brought any of their\belongings, leave them on the table.":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1360 GOSUB 6130:BM$="David spread the cloth with the crest on the table, and spoke up.":GOSUB 5100
1370 BM$="David: I want to find the owner of the coat of arms embroidered on this\handkerchief. Unfortunately, I don't know anything about this person.":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1380 BM$="Michael: Just from this piece of cloth? Hmmm...":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1390 BM$="Susanna: I guess it's impossible just from the crest...":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1400 GOSUB 9050:GOSUB 6120:GOSUB 6124:BM$="Michael: Silence, woman!\I could easily find out with my dark arts, but I would extinguish yet\another one of the lights of my life if I were to do so.":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1410 BM$="Susanna: If it's a matter of money, we have it. How much?":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1420 BM$="Michael: Do you think I'd exchange my very life for money? I have more\money than I'd ever need.\I won't use my magick for someone who ignores the value of life! Leave!":GOSUB 5100
1424 GOSUB 6120:GOSUB 6123:GOSUB 6125
1425 BM$="The flame of the candle swayed violently.":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1430 BM$="Susanna: Mr. Michael, if you truly are a sorcerer as you claim, would you\refuse to help us after seeing us in person?":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1440 COMMON FO:GOSUB 6100:BM$="The black curtains moved. Michael was apparently looking at Susanna and\David.":GOSUB 5100
1445 BM$="Michael let out a gasp.":GOSUB 5100
1450 BM$="Michael: My apologies. I shall proceed to use my dark magicks.":GOSUB 5100
1460 BM$="David was going to ask Susanna about the sudden change in Michael's\attitude, but he was interrupted before he could.":GOSUB 5100
1470 W5=0:GOSUB 9020:GOSUB 6120:BM$="Michael: I will attempt to follow the residual thoughts on this cloth, but I\cannot do this by myself. I must borrow your energy waves.":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1480 BM$="Susanna: Our...energy waves? I don't get it, but if it helps us solve the\mystery of this crest, go ahead.":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1490 BM$="Michael: Thank you. I shall now follow the residual thoughts, and send you\what I perceive.":GOSUB 5100
1500 BM$="Michael: Abandon all trivial thoughts and open your mind. Let us begin.":GOSUB 5100
1510 GOSUB 9070:GOSUB 6100:BM$="Once he could no longer hear Michael's voice, David felt some kind of\`weight` in his mind. He thought to himself that he was receiving Michael's\thoughts.":GOSUB 5100
1520 GOSUB 9070:GOSUB 9525:BM$="David tried to focus on this weight, but nothing seemed to happen. Then,\he started feeling drained, for some reason.":GOSUB 5100
1530 GOSUB 9070:BM$="Then, he heard Michael's voice. Or rather, his voice resonated within his\head.":GOSUB 5100
1535 GOSUB 6120
1540 GOSUB 9070:BM$="Michael: The ancestors of the owner of this cloth betrayed the Devil King.\They'll be rewarded with eternal happiness in the Kingdom of God, but\they've hidden their history, and coat of arms, fearing the dark":GOSUB 5100:BM$="retribution.":GOSUB 5100
1550 GOSUB 9070:BM$="Michael: I've identified the residual thoughts. I should be able to track\them to their source.":GOSUB 5100
1560 GOSUB 9070:BM$="David was now convinced that he was in one of his dreams, but unlike the\other times, he now wanted to see where it would lead.":GOSUB 5100
1562 GOSUB 9090:GOSUB 6140:BM$="Michael: Do you see it?":GOSUB 5100
1564 GOSUB 6150:BM$="Michael: This is the building I see in my mind.":GOSUB 5100
1570 GOSUB 9080:GOSUB 6160:BM$="Michael: Do you see it? This magnificent building is the source of the coat\of arms. I shall now confirm its location.":GOSUB 5100
1580 GOSUB 9070:BM$="David observed the building pictured in his mind. It was some kind of castle...":GOSUB 5100
1583 COMMON FO:GOSUB 5610:KILL I1:I1=0:CLS 2:GOSUB 6105:ISET X:BM$="The image faded from his mind.":GOSUB 5100
1590 POLL X:BM$="David could now hear Michael's voice through his ears.":GOSUB 5100
1600 BM$="Michael: This is all I can do. I hope it proves useful.":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1610 BM$="Susanna: Could you draw us a map? We have to go there.":GOSUB 5100
1620 BM$="The black curtain swayed, and a slip of paper came out of the gap. Susanna\took it, and handed over a large sum of money in return.":GOSUB 5100
1630 BM$="Susanna: We're done here. Let's go, David.":GOSUB 5100
1640 BM$="As he grabbed Susanna's hand, David chuckled bitterly to himself, thinking\it felt very realistic for a dream.":GOSUB 5100:COMMON FO
